(1)    20FC :                    ;;; An 80296SA can take an interrupt inside a call, after the call pushed
(1)    20FC :                    ;;; its return address: it pushes that address again, and the handler
(1)    20FC :                    ;;; returns past the callee. So code running with interrupts enabled
(1)    20FC :                    ;;; disables them before each call, and the callee enables them again.
(1)    20FC :                    ;;; (The 80C196NP is not checked yet.)
(1)    20FC :                    loop:
